{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJvDufwimTktGfD6V9ao","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `matplotlib.__version_info__`, a namedtuple shaped like `sys.version_info`, so version checks can compare tuples (`matplotlib.__version_info__ >= (3, 4, 2)`) instead of strings. The four tests in `test_matplotlib.py` pass, and I checked the parsing by hand on a few sample version strings.\n\n**What changed in `lib/matplotlib/__init__.py`:**\n- **New tuple type:** `_VersionInfo` has the fields `major, minor, micro, releaselevel, serial`.\n- **Parser:** `_parse_to_version_info()` turns a version string into that tuple:\n  - A plain release like `3.5.0` becomes `(3, 5, 0, 'final', 0)`.\n  - A dev build like `3.5.0.dev820+g…` becomes `(3, 5, 0, 'alpha', 820)`.\n  - `a`, `b` and `rc` pre-releases become `alpha`, `beta` and `candidate`, so `3.5.0rc2` gives `(3, 5, 0, 'candidate', 2)`.\n  - A post-release like `3.5.0.post820` is treated as a dev build of the next micro version: `(3, 5, 1, 'alpha', 820)`.\n- **Lookup:** I moved the existing version-lookup code into `_get_version()`. Both `__version__` and `__version_info__` are still worked out only on first access and then cached.\n\nIn this checkout, `__version_info__` comes out as `(0, 0, 1, 'alpha', 1)` and `__version__` as `0.0.post1+…`. That's because the repo has no git tags to read a version from, not because of the new code.\n\nI also added a short what's-new note in `doc/users/next_whats_new/version_info.rst`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":403,"cache_read_input_tokens":23043,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":403},"output_tokens":597,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7729ed60-1fbe-4345-a8d9-95f0542c2cee","uuid":"4af8b4fe-5a6c-4e57-b22c-6bde167103c3","timestamp":"2026-11-23T00:32:32.351Z","request_id":"req_011ChJvDuWGGLDcAbr1cczWc"}
